l,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;;font-size:16px\">Up until a few weeks ago, the function was providing Bayesian p-values both overall and per species, as expected. However, recently, I&#39;ve noticed a change in the output. The current output now includes species richness per station, and running the exact same code results in a different output. I have the outputs presented in R Markdown HTML format, making it clear that there is a difference, even when using identical code (see attached images).</p><p style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;margin:1.25em 0px;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-family:Söhne,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Ubuntu,Cantarell,&quot;Noto Sans&quot;,sans-serif,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;;font-size:16px\"><br></p><p style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;margin:1.25em 0px;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-family:Söhne,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Ubuntu,Cantarell,&quot;Noto Sans&quot;,sans-serif,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Noto Color Emoji&quot;;font-size:16px\"><img alt=\"WhatsApp Image 2024-03-06 à 09.20.17_d65500bd.jpg\" width=\"534px\" height=\"231px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/camtrapr/attach/3edd09bde55fc/WhatsApp%20Image%202024-03-06%20%C3%A0%2009.20.17_d65500bd.jpg?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"><br></p><p style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;margin:1.25em 0px;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-family:Söhne,ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Roboto,Ubuntu,Cantarell,&quot;Noto Sans&quot;,sans-serif,&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;,Arial,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe